 "about": "FAA-292 (DEC-0155 RT-2) and FAA-272: this OS account's own sockets and the two proofs read from them, for fabric_socket_proof.py and fabric-socket-proof.mjs. `records` are proc_pidfdinfo(PROC_PIDFDSOCKETINFO) records (struct socket_fdinfo, 792 bytes) captured on macOS 26.6 from a connected pair, an IPv6 listener and a UDP socket of one process, with every byte the module does not read zeroed and the ports and socket handles replaced; only the Python twin reads them (libproc). `lsof` are texts of `lsof -nP -a -u <uid> -iTCP:<port> -sTCP:<state> -F pun` as macOS 26.6 prints them, the first captured, the rest written in its format; both twins read them. `questions` hold this account's sockets and what each proof answers; both twins answer them. Every expectation is stated by hand.",
